course: dictionary
lesson: 1757
title: Clay and what it can become
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Clay is a noun, a name for a thing. Its clues come from the words around it. «Scribes pressed a cut reed into wet clay, making wedge-shaped marks.» You press things into soft materials, so wet clay must be soft enough to take a mark.
explain: «Almost everything in your pencil case was made by machines: a pencil is a rod of baked graphite and clay.» Baked means cooked in heat, so clay is something that can be baked. Ask yourself: what would this word need to mean for the sentence to make sense? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check.
explain: Some clues show a word's job. «A house's foundations are concrete under the walls.» Clay is not mentioned there, but «houses on clay can move a little in very dry summers, because the clay shrinks» shows that clay is ground that can change shape as it dries.
fact: Clay is soft, sticky earth that you can shape with your hands.
fact: When clay is dried or baked, it goes hard.
fact: Clay is used for pots, bricks, tiles and models.
fact: Clay soil is heavy soil that holds water.
fact: «The Terracotta Army» near Xi'an was found in 1974 by farmers digging a well; its thousands of life-size clay soldiers have different faces and hairstyles.
fact: Scribes long ago pressed a cut reed into wet clay to make wedge-shaped marks; the word «cuneiform» means wedge-shaped.
exercise: «Scribes pressed a cut reed into wet clay.» What is clay in this sentence? | Dry sand on a beach | A kind of cloth for clothes | *Soft earth you can press marks into | Hard metal used to make swords
exercise: A potter has 12 kilograms of clay and makes 4 equal pots. How much clay goes into each pot? | 8 kilograms | *3 kilograms | 4 kilograms | 2 kilograms
exercise: «Clay soil is heavy soil that holds water.» What does clay soil do? | *Holds water | Floats on top of the sea | Burns quickly like paper | Blows away in the wind
test: What is a pencil partly made of, according to «Almost everything in your pencil case was made by machines»? | Feathers and string | *Baked graphite and clay | Wool and rubber | Glass and sugar
test: Which thing is made from baked clay? | Wooden spoon | *A brick | Glass of milk | Rubber band
exam: Mia says clay and sand are the same. What is the best reply? | Clay is a kind of metal used for swords | They are exactly the same, so there is nothing to explain | Clay is always the colour of the sky | *Clay is soft, sticky earth that you can shape, and it goes hard when baked or dried
